I'm sorry, but I really, really hate the Windows Nethack interface.

In fact I know of no one (who I know in real life who plays the game,
and I'm responsible for at least three such people) who likes it!  I
hate every windowed version of Nethack I've ever seen.  It opens many
windows, uses those clunky radio buttons, the map window tends to get
hidden by lots of stuff, when you call up the inventory window you
have to manually close it, blah blah blah.  It's hideous.

It's strange.  I understand that all those menus and stuff might
possibly make it easier for a new player to learn the game, but I
think they're even scarier to a Nethack newbie than learning all those
keypresses!

While you can build a Windows console version of the game, you won't
get tiles if you do so.  That's why I still play MS-DOS Nethack even
now, you get tiles and no damnable windows.  If someone knows how to
get a non-UI-nightmare Windows Nethack with graphics let me know.

Of course, it might be possible to compile MS-DOS Nethack with MinGW
or Cygwin, but the README and files referred to by it make no mention
of that.  The MS-DOS instructions only mention using DJGPP.

Finally, before I tried using DJGPP I tried using Cygwin.  In addition
to having to download and install a *lot* of tools and other programs
that had nothing to do with building Nethack, I also ran into the same
filename problem I had with DJGPP, apparently because the source
assumes only people running MS-DOS would want to build DOS Nethack.

Sorry if this comes across as being a little ranty.  Time for Prozac!

